  "boundaries": [
    "Existing root-leaf and nonempty-partition paths and equal-cardinality update rewrite remain; no-retirement operations do not demand global allocator metadata.",
    "Every nonempty node preserves original height and actual bounded/tail form. Empty nonroot pages retire; fully empty tree reuses original root as a height-zero leaf. No speculative nonempty root promotion.",
    "Owned map containers require owner0; fixed global page1,row0 container requires owner1. Existing inline/indirect representation only; missing cells, pointer changes, row/map growth or re-encoding overflow refuse atomically.",
    "All touched-table data-owned and index-owned pages, selected definition, reserved header, and participating map containers/bitmaps must be allocated in the qualified global map. This is not a database-wide allocator coherence proof.",
    "Physical aliases deduplicate. Cross-index/data ownership overlap, retired root/storage and contradictory same-byte edits refuse. Byte patches aggregate before application, preserving every other bit including valid beyond-EOF global bits.",
    "Whole-tree surviving leaf links repaired, exact key-plus-row maxima retained; retired first four bytes zero and all remaining body bytes unchanged. Standard structure/constraint/preservation checks precede independent final map/root/storage/residual audits.",
    "Plain subversion-zero ACE16 feature-only non-journalable candidate; relationship, data-macro/history/property, ignored-NULL and normal-write gates unchanged. No allocation, INSERT, long-value reclamation or ordinary ACE write capability.",
    "Original public-writer candidate replay is separate and unrun in this implementation record. Synthetic/reference observations are not native Microsoft Access SQL/save/reopen qualification."
